---
layout: layouts/base.njk
templateClass: o-resume
title: Resume — Tylen St Hilaire
description: The résumé of Tylen St Hilaire, Head of Experience Design at CreateFuture — a design leader building AI-native product practices.
---
{#- Content lives in _data/resume.js; sections render here in the order they are
    written there.

    One column, on screen and on paper alike: header, statement, then sections of
    entries. Each entry leads with its title, followed by a meta line naming the
    organisation and period, then its points. Entries with no title of their own
    (skills, languages) read as a label and its text on one line — see
    `.c-resume__entry:not(:has(...))` in the components layer. -#}

<div class="o-col12 c-resume">

  <header class="c-resume__identity">
    <h1 class="c-resume__wordmark"><a class="c-hero__eyebrow" href="{{ '/' | url }}">{{ resume.name }}</a></h1>
    <p class="c-resume__headline">{{ resume.headline | safe }}</p>
  </header>

  {#- A description list: the field names are content, even though both layouts
      currently run the values together as one line. -#}
  <dl class="c-resume__contact">
    {%- for item in resume.contact %}
    <dt class="c-resume__contact-field">{{ item.field }}</dt>
    <dd class="c-resume__contact-value">
      {%- if item.href %}<a href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.label }}</a>{% else %}{{ item.label }}{% endif -%}
    </dd>
    {%- endfor %}
  </dl>

  {#- Authored hidden and revealed by js/main.js, so it never shows to anyone
      who cannot act on it — without JS, ⌘P still yields the single-column
      layout, which is the safe one. Each option prints directly; the layout it
      chooses is written to the URL so a given version can be linked to. -#}
  <div class="c-print" data-print hidden>
    <button class="c-print__toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="print-options">
      <svg class="c-print__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none"
           stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"
           stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M6 9V3h12v6"/>
        <path d="M6 18H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h16a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2"/>
        <rect x="6" y="14" width="12" height="7" rx="1"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="u-visually-hidden">Print or save as PDF</span>
    </button>

    {#- Label each layout by who it is for, not what it looks like -#}
    <div class="c-print__options" id="print-options" hidden>
      <button type="button" class="c-print__option c-print__option--machine"
              data-layout="single"
              title="One column — reads correctly in applicant tracking systems">
        <svg class="c-print__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none"
             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"
             stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <rect x="4.5" y="8.5" width="15" height="11" rx="3"/>
          <path d="M12 8.5V5.25"/>
          <circle cx="12" cy="4" r="1.25"/>
          <path d="M9.5 13.25v1.5M14.5 13.25v1.5"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="u-visually-hidden">One column — recommended, reads correctly in applicant tracking systems</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="c-print__option c-print__option--human"
              data-layout="two-column"
              title="Two columns — for a human reader; scrambles in applicant tracking systems">
        <svg class="c-print__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none"
             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"
             stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <circle cx="12" cy="8" r="3.5"/>
          <path d="M5.5 20.5a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 13 0"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="u-visually-hidden">Two columns — for a human reader; scrambles in applicant tracking systems</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="c-resume__statement">{{ resume.statement }}</p>

  {%- for data in resume.sections %}
  <section class="c-resume__section">
    <h2 class="c-resume__section-title">{{ data.title | safe }}</h2>

    {%- for entry in data.entries %}
    <div class="c-resume__entry">
      {%- if entry.title %}
      <h3 class="c-resume__title">{{ entry.title | safe }}</h3>
      {%- endif %}
      <p class="c-resume__meta">
        {%- if entry.org %}<span class="c-resume__org">{{ entry.org }}</span>{% if entry.orgNote %} <span class="c-resume__org-note">({{ entry.orgNote }})</span>{% endif %}<span class="c-resume__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>{% endif -%}
        <span class="c-resume__period">{{ entry.rail | safe }}</span>
      </p>
      {%- if entry.text %}
      <p class="c-resume__text">{{ entry.text | safe }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if entry.bullets %}
      <ul class="c-resume__bullets">
        {%- for bullet in entry.bullets %}
        <li>{{ bullet | safe }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  <p class="c-resume__end-mark" aria-hidden="true">❧</p>

</div>
